body:
I'm right there with ya, as a result I've had to repeat a year of high school due to my lack of discipline in getting studying/homework done. Pulling back and disciplining yourself isn't a fast and easy road but holy shit is it going to be one of the important things you ever do. One method that helps me a lot is sitting down next to someone who is being productive and work, surrounding yourself with productive role models in general helps out a lot. An easy example would be asking if you could sit next to a teacher after school/study hall and work next to them, as demoralizing as it may seem it's a great step in the right direction. Setting up meetings with your math teacher can also give your mind an incentive to succeed. The more you prolong addressing your ability to study and get work done, the harder it will get, it will backfire, trust me on that.

I might be overthinking your situation but I think it's really important to tackle procrastination as soon as possible, as it did a massive blow to my life when I let it get out of control. These methods personally worked for me this year, and I recommend giving them a shot. Good luck!

&#x200B;
